The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says “one issue, one fix queued.”
Its rendered cause table contradicts that claim. The parser is the majority cause;
the date-hint problem was merged into it and had no ticket of its own.
These are different failure paths and need separate fixes, not just a single ticket count.

## Problems and coverage

<IncidentReview />

### Parser: shared month-first interpretation

The shared parser reads month first for day-first tenants. App and email reports,
and forms without the booking-v3 month-first hint, follow this path.
For example, `R-41200` from Harbour Dental reports 7 April becoming 4 July;
`R-41205` belongs here even though intake tagged it `hint`.
[Parser issue](https://github.com/mstelm/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

Use the tenant's date order or a validated unambiguous date format at the parsing boundary.
Test ambiguous dates and day values above twelve, without depending on the reporter's browser locale.

### Hint: booking-v3 advertises the wrong order

For day-first tenants, booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form reads input in
the tenant's date order. People following the hint therefore get a different date.
This path requires the `form` channel and booking-v3; a booking-v3 tenant's app report
is not automatically a hint problem. `R-41230` from Copper Studio belongs here despite
its intake `parser` tag. [Hint issue](https://github.com/mstelm/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

Make the displayed hint match the form's actual locale-aware reader. Test both day-first
and month-first tenants and input entered exactly as the hint instructs.
Fixing the shared parser alone does not fix this misleading instruction.

## Recheck the desk's views

These are the supplied components running against the exported data, not screenshots of prose.
Counts belong in components so a changed export changes the result.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />
<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Stop new reports being merged incorrectly

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is historical and remains unchanged.
It is replaced by [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).
The [current triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe) now requires the same demonstrated cause.
Matching subjects can have different causes; different subjects can share one cause.
Missing tenant evidence is a reason to investigate, not to merge.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Scope and limits

This review covers the supplied export through 4 October, not a live desk feed.
The original counts were observations at export time, not a promise about future arrivals.
Keep parser and hint queues separate as the desk continues working; recompute from unique
report IDs when new exports arrive. Reproduce the flagged one-day descriptions rather than
claim a new root cause from wording alone.

